            "keyPoints": [
                "The tariffs use Section 338 of the Smoot-Hawley-era Tariff Act of 1930 — never before used by any president to impose duties.",
                "Three proclamations signed July 20, 2026 cover 554 tariff lines: 439 motor-vehicle, 63 alcoholic beverage, 52 dairy.",
                "Unlike earlier measures, Section 338 duties apply even to goods that would qualify duty-free under USMCA.",
                "Carney says the US 'asked too much and offered too little,' refusing exclusive access to Canada's critical minerals.",
                "Trump cited a US$60 billion trade gap; official USTR data put the 2025 US goods deficit with Canada at US$48.3 billion.",
                "BMO estimates the new tariffs could shave about half a percentage point off Canadian growth.",
                "Canada is already diversifying: non-US exports hit an all-time high in 2025, up 17.2%.",
                "Carney has said over 85% of Canada–US trade remains tariff-free under USMCA."
